  <metadata>
    <id>namedaemon</id>
    <version>0.2.0</version>
    <title>NameDaemon</title>
    <authors>Krasen Slavov</authors>
    <owners>Krasen Slavov</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://namedaemon.com/download/</projectUrl>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/namedaemon/namedaemon-desktop</projectSourceUrl>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/namedaemon/namedaemon-desktop/tree/main/packaging/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/namedaemon/namedaemon-desktop/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://namedaemon.com/wp-content/themes/namedaemon-retro/assets/images/app/icon-512.png</iconUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/namedaemon/namedaemon-desktop/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Krasen Slavov</copyright>
    <tags>namedaemon domain domain-name domain-checker watchlist freeware</tags>
    <summary>Check .com domain names in bulk, keep a watchlist and get notified when one changes status.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[NameDaemon Desktop is a small, free program for people who look for .com domain names.

* Bulk check: up to 50 names at a time against a daily snapshot of the .com zone, with the registrar and the estimated drop date when known. Export the results to CSV.
* Watchlist: names are stored on your computer and re-checked every few hours. A notification tells you when a watched name changes status.
* The nine free NameDaemon tools as native pages: name generator, availability checker, domain report, score, appraisal, audit, domain health, short domains and a drop calendar.
* Tray icon, and the website's tools in a second window.
* No account, no ads, no analytics, no telemetry. A name is sent to namedaemon.com only when you check it or when the watchlist is re-checked.
* English, Spanish, French and German.

The data comes from a daily snapshot, so "not in the snapshot" does not mean a name is available: confirm with a live check and your registrar before you buy.

This package downloads the official installer from namedaemon.com and verifies its SHA-256 checksum. The program is free (MIT licence), not commercial, and has no trial period.

The installer is not code-signed yet, so Windows SmartScreen may show a warning.]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/namedaemon/namedaemon-desktop/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
